        <briefdescription>
<para>Apply cached AMS trim data to the NPD system monitors. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Iterates over all NPD system-monitor node indices. Existing monitors receive the trim data associated with the NOC power domain; absent monitors are skipped. Processing stops at the first trim-application error.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>PwrDomain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused power-domain callback argument. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused callback argument array. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>NumOfArgs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused number of callback arguments.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS when the last attempted trim succeeds; XST_FAILURE if no trim operation establishes success; or the error returned by XPm_ApplyAmsTrim() when applying trim data fails. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
